From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915/hdmi: HDMI 2.1 Quick Media Switching (QMS-VRR)

When the sink's EDID has the QMS bit (HDMI Forum VSDB or SCDB), every
frame rate it can switch to at 1080p or 2160p (23.976 to 60 Hz) is sent
on the CTA 60 Hz timing of that resolution with a longer vertical
blank. The pixel clock and the link never change, so a refresh rate
change only changes the vertical total (the LRR fastset path) and the
sink switches without dropping the picture. Rates such as 23.976 need a
fractional number of lines per frame; a small kernel thread per pipe
alternates the vertical total every frame to hold the exact average.

Every frame carries a VTEM packet (Extended Metadata, HDMI Forum data
set 1) with QMS_EN set, in the gamut metadata DIP. A rate change is
announced with M_CONST cleared for four frames.

The requested timing is replaced by the base timing before the link is
computed, so the TMDS clock, the AVI VIC and the Dolby Vision checks
describe the signal that is sent. i915.qms=0 turns it off (0644, from
the next modeset).

Limits:
- HDR: only when the 60 Hz base gets the same bpc as the requested
  timing (intel_hdmi_compute_bpc on both clocks). 2160p50/59.94/60 and
  1080p at 10 bpc keep QMS; 2160p24/25/30 HDR at 10 bpc keeps its own
  timing. From big-fella (linux-9911): KWin's HDR desktop at 2160p60
  already runs at 8 bpc, and every rate change there was a blank.
- the Dolby Vision tunnel in its dolby-vision format at 2160p: only if
  the sink's Dolby block allows 2160p60 (the base timing);
- not on LSPCON ports (gen9/10: the VTEM does not fit the 32-byte GMP
  DIP).

Validation carried over: Tiger Lake with an LG G5 (YBLOD 0.3.3): HDR10
2160p59.94 as QMS on the 60 Hz base, Dolby Vision 23.976 over QMS with a
flip every vblank. Known problem (YBLOD 0.2.5, 2026-10-12): on the N150
with its LG TV an SDR title at 2160p 23.976 Hz went out as the 594 MHz
base with a vertical total of 5630 and was shown misaligned, with a
green line and flashing garbage; with i915.qms=0 the picture was
correct. Dolby Vision 24p titles looked fine there.

Regrouped from linux-9910-yblod-hdmi-qms,
linux-9911-big-fella-qms-hdr-8bpc and the QMS lines of
linux-9928-big-fella-tunnel-format and linux-9931-lspcon-ls-dv.

Changed since YBLOD 0.4.1:
- the exclusion for DVBRIDGE_HDR10_DEEP_COLOR went with that property
  (linux-9904-hdr10-conversion, dropped: Kodi has not set it since 0.4.0
  and amdgpu never had it).
